# Forge React Router (framework mode) .dockerignore.
#
# Allowlist, like the sibling templates — but the allowed set is different in
# kind. The SPA image needs one directory (the pre-built static bundle at
# ./dist); this image needs BOTH halves of the React Router build output
# (build/client + build/server) plus the manifest + lockfile pair the deps
# stage installs production dependencies from.
#
# build/ is therefore explicitly ADMITTED — copying the spa-react-vite
# allowlist verbatim would exclude the server bundle and produce an image
# whose CMD has nothing to run.
#
# Everything else is excluded so the context transfer stays small and
# unrelated edits do not bust the buildx cache: app/ and public/ are inputs
# to `react-router build` and are already folded into build/, node_modules is
# rebuilt production-only inside the image, and .git/.github/.env* must never
# enter a published image.
*
!build/
!package.json
!package-lock.json
